 flavor to chicken before cooking.\n[[Category:Marinade recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken]]\n== Ingredients ==\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] ({{convert|125|ml|USoz|abbr=on|disp=s}}) [[Cookbook:Chicken Broth|chicken broth]]\n* ¾ cup ({{convert|185|ml|USoz|abbr=on|disp=s}}) [[Cookbook:White Wine|white wine]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Lemon Pepper|lemon pepper]]\n* 3 tbsp [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n* ¼ cup ({{convert|85|g|oz|abbr=on|disp=s}}) [[Cookbook:Honey|honey]]\n* 2 tbsp minced [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* 3 sprigs [[Cookbook:Rosemary|rosemary]], finely chopped\n* ¼ cup ({{convert|60|ml|USoz|abbr=on|disp=s}}) extra-virgin [[Cookbook:Olive Oil|olive oil]]\n* 1 tbsp finely grated [[Cookbook:Lemon zest|lemon zest]]\n* 10 sprigs [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]], finely chopped\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Black Pepper|black pepper]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine all ingredients in a gallon size zip-top bag.\n#Refrigerate for up to 2 weeks before using to marinate chicken.\n#To use, proceed as directed in given recipe OR submerge chicken in marinade and let rest for several hours in the fridge before cooking.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Do not store and/or reuse this marinade once it has been in contact with raw meat.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wine]]\n[[Category:Recipes using honey]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using thyme]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon pepper]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Chicken Marinade","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ cup () chicken broth","sourceText":"½ cup () chicken broth","amountText":"½ cup () chicken broth","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBindin